{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"6da1a27383dd0034","name":"card_unit_dornier_do_18g","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/CovertOp/units/card_unit_dornier_do_18g","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DORNIER DO 18G","text":"Units you deploy move into the frontline, if possible.","flavorText":"The Dornier Do 18G was a German flying boat used by the Luftwaffe during WWII. The aircraft was designed as a long-range maritime patrol aircraft, but it was also used in search and rescue and weather reconnaissance missions. By the start of the war, the Dornier Do 18 was already outdated, but being the only military flying boat available, 62 of them were distributed across five Coastal aviation groups, each receiving a squadron for North Sea reconnaissance duties. However, by 1941 only one squadron still operated on Do 18 aircraft, while others had been replaced with the Blohm & Voss BV 138. A total of 170 Do 18 were built, including civilian variants. Notably, a Do 18 holds the unfortunate distinction of being the first German aircraft downed by the British during the war.","faction":"Germany","type":"fighter","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":2,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_dornier_do_18g","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_dornier_do_18g_title","SourceString":"DORNIER DO 18G","LocalizedString":"DORNIER DO 18G"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":2,"defense":5,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_dornier_do_18g_text","SourceString":"Units you deploy move into the frontline, if possible.","LocalizedString":"Units you deploy move into the frontline, if possible."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_dornier_do_18g_history","SourceString":"The Dornier Do 18G was a German flying boat used by the Luftwaffe during WWII. The aircraft was designed as a long-range maritime patrol aircraft, but it was also used in search and rescue and weather reconnaissance missions. By the start of the war, the Dornier Do 18 was already outdated, but being the only military flying boat available, 62 of them were distributed across five Coastal aviation groups, each receiving a squadron for North Sea reconnaissance duties. However, by 1941 only one squadron still operated on Do 18 aircraft, while others had been replaced with the Blohm & Voss BV 138. A total of 170 Do 18 were built, including civilian variants. Notably, a Do 18 holds the unfortunate distinction of being the first German aircraft downed by the British during the war.","LocalizedString":"The Dornier Do 18G was a German flying boat used by the Luftwaffe during WWII. The aircraft was designed as a long-range maritime patrol aircraft, but it was also used in search and rescue and weather reconnaissance missions. By the start of the war, the Dornier Do 18 was already outdated, but being the only military flying boat available, 62 of them were distributed across five Coastal aviation groups, each receiving a squadron for North Sea reconnaissance duties. However, by 1941 only one squadron still operated on Do 18 aircraft, while others had been replaced with the Blohm & Voss BV 138. A total of 170 Do 18 were built, including civilian variants. Notably, a Do 18 holds the unfortunate distinction of being the first German aircraft downed by the British during the war."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Trigger"],"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/CandidateArtwork/t_dornire_do_18.t_dornire_do_18","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Bot","artist":"Roy Huxley","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DORNIER_DO_18G.DORNIER_DO_18G